<%- include('partials/head', { pageTitle, metaDescription, canonicalPath }) %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">About</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>About AESTHETICNOVA</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-1">Heavy metal, quiet design, honest claims.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What we make</h2>
        <p>
          AESTHETICNOVA makes rings, chains, pendants, bracelets and earrings in stainless steel, plus a small
          streetwear accessories line. Every piece is designed in-house and finished by hand in small runs in India.
        </p>
        <p>
          Stainless steel is the whole idea. It is dense, it takes a polish, and it does not depend on a thin
          plating layer that turns dull in a month. When you hold one of our rings you should be able to feel the
          metal, not a coating.
        </p>

        <h2 id="claims">Our product claims policy</h2>
        <p>
          This is the part most jewellery sites skip. Here is exactly what we will and will not say about our
          products:
        </p>
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">Claims we make versus claims we avoid and why</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Claim</th><th scope="col">Our position</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>“Stainless steel”</td>
              <td><strong>Made.</strong> This is the material we buy and specify. The grade is stated where we have
                supplier documentation for it; where we do not, we say “stainless steel” and nothing more specific.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“316L stainless steel”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made as a blanket claim.</strong> We will state the grade per product only when our
                supplier certificate confirms it. Our current supplier documentation does not cover every style.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“Hypoallergenic”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made.</strong> Allergy is individual, and this is a medical-adjacent claim we cannot
                substantiate. If you have a known metal sensitivity, ask us before ordering and we will tell you
                what our supplier documentation says.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“Nickel-free”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made.</strong> Stainless steel alloys commonly contain nickel. We will not claim
                otherwise without test reports.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“Waterproof” / “tarnish-proof”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made.</strong> Our care guidance tells you what we actually recommend: dry the piece
                after wear, avoid chlorinated water and harsh cleaners. Steel is durable, but “proof” against every
                condition is a promise we cannot keep.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“Lifetime guarantee”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made.</strong> What you get is the statutory rights described in our
                <a href="/terms">Terms</a> and <a href="/returns">Refund Policy</a>, plus our stated care guidance.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>“Certified” / “medically safe”</td>
              <td><strong>Not made.</strong> We hold no such certification, so we display none.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>What we do measure</h2>
        <p>
          Because claims are limited, we invest in the boring, useful details instead: millimetre widths, exact
          weights at a stated size, chain lengths end-to-end including the clasp, and the finish on each face.
          These are on every product page in the “Details &amp; measurements” panel.
        </p>

        <h2 id="pricing">How our pricing works</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every listed price includes GST at 18%. The tax component is itemised in your order summary.</li>
          <li>Shipping is a flat ₹79, free over ₹1,499, and it is shown in your bag <em>before</em> you pay.</li>
          <li>Cash on delivery, if enabled, adds a ₹49 fee that appears in the total the moment you select it.</li>
          <li>We do not run fake countdowns or invented “was” prices. If we ever show a crossed-out price, it will be
            the lowest price offered in the previous 30 days, per the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) (Amendment)
            Rules, 2026. Right now we do not run discounts, so there are no crossed-out prices on this site.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="reviews">Reviews</h2>
        <p>
          We do not seed reviews, buy reviews or write them ourselves. A review can only be submitted by a signed-in
          customer with a real order for that product, and the “verified purchase” label is calculated from that
          order. When a product has no reviews, the page says so.
        </p>

        <h2>Made in, and who sells it</h2>
        <p>
          Country of origin is listed on every product page. AESTHETICNOVA sells directly to consumers — there is no
          third-party marketplace seller in between. Seller and business details, including the grievance officer,
          are on the <a href="/business-details">business details page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Where we are honest about being new</h2>
        <p>
          This is a new store in a fresh build. Our catalogue is real and our stock numbers are real, but we have not
          manufactured a history: no invented review counts, no “10,000 happy customers”, no fake press logos.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<%- include('partials/consent-banner') %>
</body>
</html>
